                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "\"Towers of Altrac\" was an unusual semi-professionally developed co-op fantasy themed tower defense game from Russia.  It's pretty generic stuff and the quality was considered D minus tier shovelware... back in 2015.  It hasn't been maintained at all, there's no players, so this leaves you with the option to buy a co-op game that you have to play alone... not appealing.\n\nThe controls and gameplay and overall general design is quite poor, and that's before you take the sloppy Russian translation into account.  This is unpleasant to play, and not just because of how old it is.  The game wasn't successful in 2015 and it's completely unrecommendable now.\n\nOn the upside, the game does feature customisable controls and resolution, so at least some of the basic, minimum requirements have been met.  Unfortunately there's a number of other technical defects and shortcomings which contribute to the game being difficult to recommend to gamers.\n\nDue to the age of this game, and the lack of modernisation, the graphics appear quite dated.  This compares poorly to more contemporary games with professional standards.  Given that gaming is primarily a visual medium, this is a bit of a problem, so should be taken into account when considering whether to get this game.\n\nThese technical defects push this game below acceptable standards for any modern PC game.\n\nNow on to pricing and value for gamers.  So, should you buy this game?  Is this one of the best of the 140,000+ games on Steam?\n\nTowers of Altrac - Epic Defense Battles is relatively cheap at $1 USD, but it's not worth it.  This is also competing with over 14,000 free games available on Steam, many of them far better than this paid product.\n\nThe quality problems and defects with this game makes the asking price totally unrealistic. It's impossible to recommend this to gamers here on Steam.\n",
